{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "070N", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\mathcal{C}, \\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0005": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\ldots \\ar[r] &\n\\tau_{\\geq -2}\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet \\ar[r] \\ar[d] &\n\\tau_{\\geq -1}\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet \\ar[d] \\\\\n\\ldots \\ar[r] & \\mathcal{I}_2^\\bullet \\ar[r] & \\mathcal{I}_1^\\bullet\n}\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{I}_n^\\bullet$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{I}_{n + 1}^\\bullet \\to \\mathcal{I}_n^\\bullet$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{I}^\\bullet = \\lim_n \\mathcal{I}_n^\\bullet$", "MATH_0011": "\\begin{equation}\n\\label{equation-into-candidate-K-injective}\n\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet \\to \\mathcal{I}^\\bullet\n\\end{equation}", "REF_0001": "\\ref{derived-lemma-special-inverse-system}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{derived-lemma-bounded-below-injectives-K-injective}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{derived-lemma-limit-K-injectives}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c74bd42a43feeb793e2ad7022df354c5888829f3f9162e3d4c831aa7859c14ed", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:af83265ae51e2b4baddd51be738378de6f4c74abbc1823e04551d2b3e2992718", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a ringed site.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a complex of <MATH_0003>-modules.\nThe category <MATH_0004> has enough injectives, hence\nwe can use\nDerived Categories, Lemma <REF_0001>\nproduce a diagram\n<MATH_0005>\nin the category of complexes of <MATH_0006>-modules such that\n<STRUCT_0002>\n<STRUCT_0003> the vertical arrows are quasi-isomorphisms,\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0007> is a bounded below complex of injectives,\n<STRUCT_0005> the arrows <MATH_0008>\nare termwise split surjections.\n<STRUCT_0006>\nThe category of <MATH_0009>-modules has limits (they are computed\non the level of presheaves), hence we can form the termwise limit\n<MATH_0010>. By\nDerived Categories, Lemmas\n<REF_0002> and\n<REF_0003>\nthis is a K-injective complex. In general the canonical map\n<MATH_0011>\nmay not be a quasi-isomorphism. In the following lemma we describe some\nconditions under which it is.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6e53493c169ef36bbeb91ec93424da56b92788e39a7dc681cd49b7c00fc9f945", "unit_id": "tag:070N:prose-0001"}
