{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "070N", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet \\to R\\lim \\tau_{\\geq -n} \\mathcal{F}^\\bullet$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{derived-lemma-difficulty-K-injectives}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-is-limit-dimension}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9e149a98eefea906bd304126f506152be4509b71749f0314ab635bbd0081ee85", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:73ac3b6010e124aab0b9cf0d7e67e7a87ec3857c947544781e391efb8aed5a07", "source_text": "By Derived Categories, Lemma <REF_0001>\nit suffices to show that the map\n<MATH_0001>\nis an isomorphism. This follows from Lemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:afc980a545845ff4da6b1681806a098365c0af8a7ae9122fde1acf47e7d60d96", "unit_id": "tag:070Q:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "070N", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:de23b9536706f5e60ef390ffe1768f7c44ad20e7b5cb76110b14c59c4ce62b84", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nHere is a technical lemma about cohomology sheaves of termwise limits of\ninverse systems of complexes of modules. We should avoid using this lemma\nas much as possible and instead use arguments with derived inverse\nlimits.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:07a6d9732342b382c65798e804d19bf382e7013adee61e144f694e77b59b73a3", "unit_id": "tag:070N:prose-0002"}
